Welcome to SeaAwardBIOS!

This project is based on SeaBIOS and is designed to emulate the look and
behavior of an Award BIOS-style firmware for x86 legacy systems. In addition
to the standard SeaBIOS foundation, it includes Award-like BIOS features and
compatibility elements such as:

  - NVARM support
  - CMOS Setup configuration interface
  - SCSI BIOS Display support

The code is built with standard GNU tools and is intended for classic BIOS
platforms, firmware development, and QEMU-based testing.

Quick build and test:

  make
  qemu -bios out/bios.bin

SeaAwardBIOS can be configured with kconfig. To adjust the default
configuration, run:

  make menuconfig
  make

For more build notes and project documentation, please refer to the files in
the docs/ directory and the source tree.
